                        <cell>C. USN</cell>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell> NSA DaNang Support</cell>
                        <cell role="num">1775</cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>D. Total MACV </cell>
                        <cell role="num">30000</cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>The Secretary of the Army proposes to meet the request for a mechanized brigade
                    by deploying a brigade from the 5th Mechanized Division. He now believes it
                    cannot be ready to deploy before 12 July.</p>
                <pb facs="0427" n="383" xml:id="pg383"/>
                <p>Moreover, for the reasons noted earlier, I would like to substitute an Army
                    infantry brigade and support personnel for the 27th Regimental Landing Team and
                    support personnel that deployed in February. Therefore, I would propose to
                    substitute 7,363 Army personnel for Marines in the first half of July. The Army
                    can provide the personnel; the Secretary of the Navy now believes the 27th RLT
                    can be sustained until then.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d127-f2"/></p>
                <p>Would you please inform General Westmoreland of these proposals, and of my
                    preference for them, and ask him whether he considers the substitutions
                        satisfactory.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d127-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed>Paul H. Nitze </signed></closer>
